{
  "id": "specific-variance",
  "term": "specific variance",
  "definition": "In this packet, specific variance refers to the part of a measure that can be separated from other sources of variation and linked to a particular source, such as stable individual differences. It is contrasted with variance due to the measurement occasion, the methods used, or measurement error.",
